Density source: RI fit of 126 orbitals, 182 auxiliary functions.
  rho and its gradient come from one pass over the auxiliary functions, N_aux per point instead of
  N_basis x N_MO, so grids of 0.05 A and finer are affordable. The QTAIM basins and populations below
  are those of the fitted density: it matches the orbital density to ~1e-3 e/bohr^3 at bond critical
  points, and its tail (rho < 0.01) is not reliable. ELI-D is taken from the orbitals.
[ELI (PC07)] Perdew & Constantin, Phys. Rev. B 75 (2007) 155109, DOI 10.1103/PhysRevB.75.155109
